\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rally pauses, Taiwan dlr off 7-mth hi.  \b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2004\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In SINGAPORE story "Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -Rally pauses, Taiwan\par dlr off 3-=   yr high" please read headline in part as "Taiwan\par dlr off 7-mth high" instead of "Taiwan dlr off 3-=   yr high".\par     Please read paragraph 1 in part as "after strengthening to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a seven-month-high" instead of "to a three-and-half-year high"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 and paragraph 2 in part as "32.80 per dollar in early trades"  \par \par \uc2 instead of "32.62 per dollar in offshore trades". (Corrects  \par \par \uc2 erroneous exchange rate quote and time comparison).   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      A corrected story follows.\par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar steadied on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday after strengthening to a seven-month high, while other  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  backed off multi-year highs on concerns  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 central banks would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the rally.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar gained to 32.80 per dollar in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 early trades before shedding some its gains. The South Korean  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won traded close to its seven-year high of 1,091 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar reached on Monday and the Singapore dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 retreated from a near five-year high of 1.6488 per dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Traders were concerned about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par across Asia, led by Japan, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Singapore and Taiwan.\par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have rallied since the start of October as\par the U.S. dollar weakened against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over\par persistent concerns about the U.S. budget and trade deficits.\par     "While the longer-term trend of a weaker dollar remains\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 intact, here and there we're going to find people getting  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cautious," said Song Seng Wun, economist at G.K. Goh Securities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I won't be surprised to see some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 central banks across the region. They don't want to see one-way  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 traffic in too short a time."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banks and stock markets in Singapore, the Philippines and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India reopened Tuesday after a three-day weekend including  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday's holiday for Eid-al-Fitri. Indonesia is closed all  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Korean won has strengthened 5.5 percent against the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar since the start of October, while the Taiwan dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has gained nearly 4 percent and the Singapore dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has appreciated over 2 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are helping the region curb\par imported inflation from oil and other commodities in check.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, which steers monetary\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policy through the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has maintained its stance of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gradual and modest appreciation in the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the second quarter of this year as it seeks to control  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In South Korea, a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped keep a lid on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 prices of imported oil and other commodities and enabled the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates last week to revive growth  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and stimulate domestic consumer demand.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil, which was trading on the New York Mercantile  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exchange's electronic market on Tuesday around $46.70 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 barrel, remains a concern for Asian policy makers, said Song.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Those concerns, coupled with the view that the dollar's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weakness was broad-based, will probably moderate the level of  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Asian central banks, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen strengthened to a seven-month high against  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the dollar on Monday, before giving up some ground. The euro  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has lost some 0.5 percent since touching a record high of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 $1.3006 last week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They can't lean against the wind," said Song.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Speculators continue to hold on to euro-longs, yen-longs,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 taking a view that the dollar is on a weakening trend."   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0309 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.37         105.28       -0.09\par  Sing dlr        1.6519         1.6500       -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      32.821         32.800       -0.06\par  Korean won     1092.60        1092.30       -0.03\par  Baht             40.39          40.33       -0.14\par  Peso             56.32          56.35       +0.05\par  Rupiah         8987.00        8980.00       -0.08\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.37         107.31       +1.84\par  Sing dlr        1.6519         1.6978       +2.78\par  Taiwan dlr      32.821         33.978       +3.53\par  Korean won     1092.60        1192.00       +9.10\par  Baht             40.39          39.59       -1.98\par  Peso             56.32          55.49       -1.47\par  Rupiah         8987.00        8410.00       -6.42\par  Rupee            45.10          45.60       +1.11.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041116e0bg003mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
