\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dlr, won surge as dlr falls.  \b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2004\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar and the\par South Korean won rose to their strongest levels in six months\par on Wednesday as an uncertain outlook for the U.S. economy and\par interest rates knocked the dollar lower against major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The dollar weakened to a seven-and-half month low against\par the euro and hit a three-month low against the yen. The yen's\par one percent gain on Wednesday helped support Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par eventhough oil was trading above $53 a barrel.\par     The Bank of Thailand raised its key 14-day repo rate by 25\par basis points to 1.75 percent, citing inflationary pressures.\par The baht was already stronger on the day and showed little\par reaction to the move, which had been expected by most analysts.\par     While the baht reached one-week highs, the Singapore\par dollar, seen as a proxy for some of Asia's biggest exporting\par countries with pegged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as China and Malaysia,\par and the won headed towards their 2004 peaks.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar and the won have been rising in the\par past two weeks after a string of weaker-than-expected U.S. data\par and on a growing U.S. trade deficit, mainly with Asia.\par  \par     "We may see more and more of these days in the future,"\par said G.K. Goh economist Song Seng Wun.\par     "We're seeing a growing school of literature arguing for a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weaker dollar. When more and more people begin doubting the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sustainability of the U.S. current account balances, that's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 where it's going to go."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  got a further boost from a Nikkei  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 newspaper report that said Japan may be nearing the end of its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deflationary years and that the Bank of Japan would likely  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forecast a rise in consumer prices next fiscal year in a report  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 due on Oct 29.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A return of inflation in Japan, which some analysts expect  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sometime next year, would mean higher interest rates and a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 return of foreign investment in Japanese property and bonds.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Performance of inflation-linked Japanese government bonds  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 will improve significantly from mid-2005," Goldman Sachs said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in a report from Tokyo.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, further gains in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be capped by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reluctance of the region's authorities to let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthen against neighbours who compete in the same export  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 markets.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulators in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Taiwan have  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  occasionally to buy dollars to stem gains in their  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The trade-weighted Singapore dollar could already be close  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to the upper end of an undisclosed band set by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary  \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, said Song.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further gains in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could also be restricted  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by the surging price of crude oil which may derail an economic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recovery in Japan and other Asian countries and restrict trade  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 demand from outside the region.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "While there are substantial signs of recovery in Japan and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the rest of Asia, every \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region is looking  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over his shoulder about what oil's doing to the region's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economies," said Song.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. oil futures have traded above $50 a barrel for most of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this month, after jumping from below $40 in June. Earlier this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week Morgan Stanley and J.P. Morgan downgraded their global  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic forecasts for 2005 because of high oil prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Officials at the Bank of Japan and other Asian countries  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 have also voiced concerns about the impact of the oil prices on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic growth.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0826 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       108.18         109.31       +1.04\par  Sing dlr        1.6720         1.6778       +0.35\par  Taiwan dlr      33.804         33.856       +0.15\par  Korean won     1142.80        1144.80       +0.18\par  Baht             41.31          41.37       +0.15\par  Peso             56.28          56.36       +0.14\par  Rupiah         9070.00        9092.00       +0.24\par  Rupee            45.76          45.81       +0.10\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       108.18         107.31       -0.80\par  Sing dlr        1.6720         1.6978       +1.54\par  Taiwan dlr      33.804         33.978       +0.51\par  Korean won     1142.80        1192.00       +4.31\par  Baht             41.31          39.59       -4.18\par  Peso             56.28          55.49       -1.40\par  Rupiah         9070.00        8410.00       -7.28\par  Rupee            45.76          45.60       -0.36.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041020e0ak005ka\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
