\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won down by noon on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2004\par 05:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     0300 GMT - South Korean won                   widens losses\par by midday, as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players chase the recently-battered U.S.\par dollar amid concerns about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par government to weaken the won.\par     - Won quoted at 1,145.2 per dollar, compared with 1,143.5 at\par Monday close, the best domestic finish since April 13 when it\par ended at 1,141.1.\par     - "Both offshore and onshore (dollar) buying strengthened\par with some importers interested in buying dollars for\par settlements," says a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer.\par     - The won has been rising steadily of late due to the\par dollar's softening against major global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But demand\par for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from sustained foreign equity sales and\par concerns about the impact of higher energy costs on weak domestic\par consumption has capped the local unit's gains.\par     - South Korea is particularly sensitive to high energy costs\par as it is the world's fourth-biggest oil buyer and has to import\par all its crude needs.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - On the economic front, South Korea's jobless rate fell in\par September for the first time in eight months, while the number of\par employed people rose to 22.57 million from 22.35 million,\par government data shows.\par     - South Korea's jobless rate is closely watched by markets\par for clues on when a two-year slump in domestic consumption, which\par has dragged on economic growth, might be coming to an end.\par     - But the market largely ignored the jobs data and players\par were instead focusing their attention on potential government\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves edged up 0.1 percent during the first half of October,\par as a softer dollar boosted the conversion value of assets in\par other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Reserves climbed to a fresh record $174.7\par billion as of mid-October versus $174.5 billion at end-September.\par     - The yen       , which the won closely follows, trading at\par 109.39/44 in Asia trade, versus 109.21 in late New York trade on\par Monday.\par     - Seoul's benchmark stock index         up 0.75 percent with\par foreign investors selling a net 46 billion won worth of stocks on\par the main bourse.\par  \par                          0300 GMT       0020 GMT       prev day\par                          (latest)      (morning)   (prev close)\par  Won                      1,145.2        1,143.7        1,143.5\par  *Yen/won              10.4487/35     10.4487/35     10.4620.31\par  ~NDF 1-mth won       1,146.5/7.5    1,145.0/6.0    1,145.2/6.2\par  ~NDF 3-mth won      1,149.6/50.6    1,148.1/9.1    1,148.3/9.3\par  Stocks KOSPI              854.56         860.34         848.27\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * calculated based on each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rates against the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ~ non-deliverable forward rates quoted by Prebon Yamane Asia  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pacific.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041019e0aj002gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172