\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won dips early,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears spread.  \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2004\par 02:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     0020 GMT - South Korean won                   dips early on\par Tuesday, retracing opening gains, as players grow more cautious\par about the prospects for government dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     - Won quoted at 1,143.7 per dollar after finishing at 1,143.5\par on Monday, the best domestic close since April 13 when it ended\par at 1,141.1.\par     - "Cautious trade due to concerns over government action will\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 limit any major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves," said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer. "But the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 dollar could turn higher if the market receives a bout of dollar  \par \par \uc2 purchase orders from recent foreign equity sales."  \par \par \uc2 - The won has been rising steadily recently due to the  \par \par \uc2 dollar's softening against major global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But demand  \par \par \uc2 for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from sustained equity sales by foreign  \par \par \uc2 investors and concerns about the impact of higher energy costs  \par \par \uc2 has capped the local unit's gains.  \par \par \uc2 - South Korea is particularly sensitive to high energy costs  \par \par \uc2 as it is the world's fourth-biggest oil buyer and has to import  \par \par \uc2 all its crude needs.  \par \par \uc2 - On the economic front, South Korea's jobless rate fell in  \par \par \uc2 September for the first time in eight months, dipping to a  \par \par \uc2 seasonally adjusted 3.5 percent from 3.6 percent in August,  \par \par \uc2 government data shows.  \par \par \uc2 - South Korea's jobless rate is closely watched by markets  \par \par \uc2 for clues on when a two-year slump in domestic consumption, which  \par \par \uc2 has dragged on economic growth, might be coming to an end.  \par \par \uc2 - But the market largely ignored the jobs data and players  \par \par \uc2 were instead focusing their attention on potential government  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 reserves edged up 0.1 percent during the first half of October,  \par \par \uc2 as a softer dollar boosted the conversion value of assets in  \par \par \uc2 other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Reserves climbed to a fresh record $174.7  \par \par \uc2 billion as of mid-October versus $174.5 billion at end-September.  \par \par \uc2 - The yen , which the won closely follows, trading at  \par \par \uc2 109.38/43 in Asia trade, versus 109.21 in late New York trade on  \par \par \uc2 Monday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Seoul's benchmark stock index         up 1.52 percent.\par                         0020 GMT      late prev day\par                        (latest)        (prev close)\par  Won                     1,143.7            1,143.5\par  *Yen/won             10.4487/35         10.4620.31\par  ~NDF 1-mth won      1,145.0/6.0        1,145.2/6.2\par  ~NDF 3-mth won      1,148.1/9.1        1,148.3/9.3\par  Stocks KOSPI             860.34             848.27\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * calculated based on each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rates against the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ~ non-deliverable forward rates quoted by Prebon Yamane Asia  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pacific.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA00000200410