\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won ends down, curbed bond plan limits loss.  \b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2004\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The South Korean won         ended domestic\par trade a shade lower on Friday, dented by a retreat in the Japanese yen\par and as state-run banks stepped in to buy the dollar in the local\par market.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But a scaled back bond issuance plan to fund the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market bolstered sentiment for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The won settled in local trade at 1,145.8 per dollar, compared with Thursday's close of 1,145.1, the highest finish in almost five months. The won was buoyed in the previous session by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave interest rates unchanged at a record low.  \par \par \uc2 The won moved between 1,144.9 and 1,147.3 during the session, dealers said. State-run banks, believed to be acting on behalf of the government, were seen chasing dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The yen , which the won closely follows, was quoted at 110.00/04, down from 109.68 posted in late New York trade.  \par \par \uc2 "But given mounting inflationary pressure and the budget ministry's move to scale back the amount of bonds to be issued for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it won't be easy for the government to actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a local bank dealer said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  planned to issue up to 21.9 trillion won in treasury bonds in 2005 to fund its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a budget ministry official said. The amount was down from the government's original plan to sell a maximum of 26.9 trillion won worth next year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers also expected more dollar sales stemming from recent\par large-scale equity sales to foreign investors involving Woori Financial\par Group  and cigarette maker KT&G\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai said on Friday he regretted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision a day earlier to leave interest rates unchanged, arguing it could have taken a more aggressive stance to support economic growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the political front, South Korea's foreign minister said on Friday it was hard to be optimistic that six-party talks on dismantling North Korea's nuclear programmes could be held in September.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors bought a net 107 billion won worth of shares on the main board, which ended up 1.76 percent at a 4-month closing high.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    0700 GMT           open    late prev day\par                       (latest)       (morning)    (prev close)\par   Won                      1,145.8         1,147.3         1,145.1\par   *Yen/won              10.4154/20      10.4933/90      10.4707/73\par   ~NDF 1-mth won       1,147.3/8.3     1,147.7/8.7     1,147.0/8.0\par   ~NDF 3-mth won       1,150.2/1.2     1,150.6/1.6     1,149.0/0.9\par   Stocks KOSPI              836.34          826.06          821.88\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * calculated based on each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rates against the dollar ~ non-deliverable forward rates quoted by Prebon Yamane Asia Pacific.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040910e09a006bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
