\par\par \b \uc2 S Korea Govt Official: Will Leave USD/KRW To Mkt Forces  \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2004\par 02:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--The South Korean government will let the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's direction be decided by market forces and doesn't plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the won's gains against the dollar, even as the won strengthens to a two-month high, a finance ministry official said Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We don't have a specific target for the dollar/won and we plan to leave the pair completely up to the market," Kim Ik-Joo, director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market division, told Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped to 1,148.2 won soon after opening Wednesday, a level not seen since July 12. It had closed at KRW1,150.8 Tuesday. [ 08-09-04 0026GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Many players had expected dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the government to defend the psychologically important KRW1,150 level, and the dollar/won lost ground early Wednesday due to the absence of such government action, participants said.  \par \par \uc2 Kim added that the government can step in to "smooth" \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  if sentiment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market excessively favors one direction, or on volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 However, he declined to comment on whether he sees such a need at the moment.  \par \par \uc2 The government has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market throughout the year, mopping up dollars in support of South Korea's trade-reliant economy amid extremely sluggish domestic demand.  \par \par \uc2 But recent government comments and actions suggest eased opposition to a stronger won on growing inflationary pressure due to high global oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 The government decided to issue KRW1 trillion in treasurys this month to fund its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , instead of an expected KRW2 trillion, even after it gained parliamentary approval to issue an extra KRW11 trillion worth of treasurys for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds this year.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's headline inflation surged to a three-year high in August, gaining 4.8% over the year.  \par \par \uc2 -By Hye-Seung Seo, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-732-2165; hyeseung.seo@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 08-09-04 0102GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040908e0980000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
