\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea counts cost of  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy, c.bank loss eyed.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik   \par \uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2004\par 06:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Sept 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may tip the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into its first loss in 10 years in 2004, government sources say, rekindling a debate over the value of a policy aimed at boosting exports.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , faced heavy interest payments on monetary stabilisation bonds it issued to fund its policy of buying dollars to cap the won's strength, the sources said.   \par \par \uc2 "The bank has probably suffered a loss in the first half and the trend could last through the rest of the year," said a government source close to the bank's balance sheet. The Bank of Korea does not release half-year balance sheet figures.   \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry argues the policy helps keep exports competitive, a rare bright spot in the economy, Asia's third largest.   \par \par \uc2 But many economists say it incurs not only huge direct costs but fails to cushion the economy from imported inflation stemming from high global oil and raw material prices.   \par \par \uc2 "In addition to the direct cost involved in the policy, its impact on the domestic inflation trend is a major problem," said Lim Ji-won, an economist at JP Morgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2 Consumer inflation hit its highest rate in over three years in the year through August.   \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry expects to pay 1.8 trillion won ($1.56 billion) in interest on this year's monetary stabilisation bonds, up a fifth from last year, an official at the ministry's international finance department said.   \par \par \uc2 The ministry plans to sell up to 18.8 trillion in bonds to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, up 47 percent from last year.   \par \par \uc2 Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paid 2.76 trillion won during the first six months of this year in interest on bonds issued to absorb increased won liquidity, a bank official said.   \par \par \uc2 The huge sums outweigh an estimated 2.6 trillion won economic stimulus package that the ruling party put forward last week.   \par \par \uc2 "The money paid as interest of course went to people who bought the bonds but a problem is that these are rich people, and the government should have spent the money on those who really want help," said Oh Suk-tae, an economist at Citigroup.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by a quarter to $170.49 billion by the end of August from a year ago, making them the fourth-biggest in the world. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and economists say much of the increase came from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The won fell 0.5 percent against the dollar in 2003, in stark contrast to a more than 10 percent gain in the Japanese yen and a nearly 20 percent rise in the euro against the dollar during the same period.   \par \par \uc2 The won has gained about 4 percent so far this year against the dollar, while the yen and euro weakened by about 2 percent and 4 percent respectively. Dealers said the won's rise was technical after last year's weakness rather than a change in policy.   \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry appeared unmoved by arguments that some of the rise in inflation stemming from high raw material prices could have been choked off by allowing the won to rise.   \par \par \uc2 "We will not intentionally use \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to solve the inflation problem," Choi Joong-kyung, head of the ministry's international finance bureau, told Reuters last week. ($1=1152.7 Won).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040908e0980040j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
