\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea bonds end flat, await next week's rate meet.   \b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2004\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     SEOUL, Sept 3 (Reuters) - South Korean government bond prices\par ended flat on Friday as doubts deepened over whether interest\par rates would be cut in September. Expectations of a cut have been\par driving a rally in a market flush with ample liquidity.\par     Bonds managed to recoup early falls after a correction over\par the last 2 days, as cash-rich investors continued to bet the Bank\par of Korea could still lower rates in coming months.\par     Strong inflation data and government measures to boost weak\par domestic demand had dampened appetite for bonds in recent\par sessions, dealers said, but some buying interest remained because\par economic fundamentals had yet to show signs of improvement.\par     "Now the market seemed to see the chance of a rate cut to be\par about 50 percent from the previous 80 percent, with investors\par taking a cautious stance ahead of next week's monetary policy\par meeting," said a fixed income analyst at a local securities firm.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yield on three-year treasury bonds\par finished unchanged at 3.62 percent. The five-year treasury bond\par yield  was down 1 basis points.\par     Expectations for further monetary easing had pushed the\par benchmark 3-year treasury yield down by almost 50 basis points\par since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly cut 25 basis points off rates\par to a record low of 3.5 percent in August.\par  \par     The Bank of Korea will hold a monetary policy meeting on\par Sept. 9.\par                                         close      prev close\par  5-yr treasury bonds                  3.78 pct       3.77 pct\par  3-yr treasury bonds                  3.62 pct       3.62 pct\par  3-yr corporate bonds                 4.16 pct       4.16 pct\par  2-yr monetary stabilisation bonds    3.61 pct       3.61 pct\par  1-yr treasury bonds                  3.52 pct       3.52 pct\par  1-yr monetary stabilisation bonds    3.52 pct       3.52 pct\par  3-mth CDs                            3.52 pct       3.52 pct\par  Average interbank call                  ~           3.65 pct\par  Average call rate                       ~           3.60 pct\par  ~ Not available\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par     Bond sentiment was supported by comments from Choi\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Joong-kyung, head of the finance ministry's international finance   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bureau. Choi said the ministry would not use \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 policy as a tool to ease growing inflationary pressure.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This was taken by investors as a sign the government may   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 avoid issuing additional treasuries to fund its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Export-driven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign   \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to keep the won cheap against the dollar in order   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to boost exporters' price competitiveness.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     On the supply front, the Finance ministry will auction 1.98\par trillion won ($1.72 billion) in three-year treasuries on Monday.\par     On the Korea Futures Exchange, the key September contract for\par three-year treasuries  closed unchanged at 112.16.\par     On the local stock market, the benchmark Korea Composite\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock Price Index was down 0.38 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1=1150.0 Won).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040903e093006k5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
