\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves up to record in July.  \b0\par\par\uc2 172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2004\par 23:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SEOUL, Aug 3 (Reuters) - South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves rose slightly to a record $168 billion at the end of\par July, mainly due to investment gains, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on\par Tuesday.\par     The reserves, the fourth-highest in the world, rose by $977\par million from $167 billion at the end of June, the Bank of Korea\par said in a statement.\par  \par     The reserves were up 8 percent, or $12.65 billion, from the\par end of 2003.\par     Dealers suspect monetary authorities have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 heavily to buy dollars and safeguard the won's export  \f28 \par \par \uc2 competitiveness, leading to a steady rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denies \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and provides few  \par \par \uc2 details of its reserves. It said 82.8 percent of reserves were  \par \par \uc2 held in securities such as U.S. Treasuries, but it did not  \par \par \uc2 elaborate.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     South Korean reserves (US$ million):\par    End-July    End-June    End-May     End-April   End-March\par     168,006     167,030     166,543     163,635     163,557.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040802e082002gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
