\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea to more than double bonds to cap won.   \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2004\par 01:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 2 (Reuters) - South Korea will more than double its planned offering of bonds to fund its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a finance ministry official said on Friday, in what is seen as showing its strong intention to keep the won cheap.   \par \par \uc2 The official said the government would seek parliament approval to raise this year's ceiling on treasury bond offerings to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 18.8 trillion won ($16.29 billion) from the previous 7.8 trillion.   \par \par \uc2 The move came as data showed a slump in domestic spending was poised to last for an extended period. That makes exports more important to keep the recovery in Asia's fourth-largest economy on track.   \par \par \uc2 "We have decided to increase the ceiling on treasuries for the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by 11 trillion won and all of them will be denominated in Korean won," the official told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 The government has never confirmed its direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but dealers suspect monetary authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to buy dollars and rein in the won to ensure South Korean exports are competitive.   \par \par \uc2 The won was almost unchanged at the end of 2003 from a year earlier against the U.S. dollar whereas the Japanese yen and euro gained sharply over the period - making the won cheaper in comparison to these major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier on Friday the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, ranked fourth in the world, rose slightly by $487 million to $167.03 billion by the end of June from the previous month.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea attributed the rise to investment gains, but dealers believe some of the rise represented \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has issued six trillion won of bonds so far out of the original 7.8 trillion won planned.   \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey showed South Korea's business sentiment dipped at an 11-month low as companies grew more pessimistic about a swift turnaround in the sluggish consumption, that began sagging at the end of 2002. ($1=1154.0 Won).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040701e0710036b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
