\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Modest gains amid stumbling blocks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2004\par 10:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, April 19 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par firmer on Monday, with the Korean won leading the pack, after\par unexpectedly weak U.S. economic data soothed fears of a\par near-term monetary tightening there and caused the yen and euro\par to rally.\par     Still, the pace of gains in the yen       , Singapore\par dollar  and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unhurried and\par reflected investor caution ahead of a Group of Seven meeting on\par the weekend and U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's\par testimony on the economy on Wednesday.\par     Some analysts said an appreciation in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par could be derailed in the longer run by any steep rise in U.S.\par rates and the threat of slower growth in China.\par     "Away from the short-term position squaring that has\par occurred on bullish Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  views, there are two real\par risks," Lehman Brothers said in a note.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The first is whether Fed tightening derails the Asian\par equity rally and the constant inflow of equity capital that has\par supported it."\par     "The second risk to Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the building signs\par of a slowdown in China, the region's engine of growth for the\par past few years," Lehman's report said, adding that it was\par however too early to be worried about China.\par  \par     The yen hovered around 108 per dollar, the dollar still up\par three yen from last week's lows.\par     The Singapore dollar        remained around 1.6770/80 per\par dollar, up about a cent from last week's lows, while the Taiwan\par dollar  settled on the firmer side of 33 per dollar.\par     The Thai baht        was in a range of 39.30 to 39.40 per\par dollar, up a percent from last week's trough.\par     Last week's consumer sentiment and industrial production\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 data in the United States was weaker than markets expected, and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 there was an easing of optimism over the economy, which had  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 driven up the expectations of the Fed hiking rates sooner.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After comments by Fed Governor Ben Bernanke and Richmond  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank President Alfred Broaddus, analysts said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 markets were preparing for Greenspan too to be cautious in his  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 statements and to play down the chances of rate hikes.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We've already had a flag on what Greenspan is going to be  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 talking about," David Simmonds, markets strategist with Royal  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Scotland, said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Simmonds said the Fed might shift its view on inflation to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suggest that the risks between inflation and disinflation were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 balanced if not tilted toward inflation, but it would still  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 convey patience on monetary policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the G7 meeting would probably be a non-event  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, given the perception that most Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 countries were allowing their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rise to ward off  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 external inflationary pressures.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "There will be a less obsessive focus on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par although China will be discussed," Simmonds said.\par     WON POLICY\par     The Korean won                   was traded around 1,153\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 per dollar, a gain of almost 10 won since Friday. It has risen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.5 percent in two months, prompting speculation that the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities have moderated their won-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell in the first  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 half of April by $600 million to $162.96 billion on April 15,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said that was due to a decline in the euro  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and yen against the dollar during that period.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "There is little doubt that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was reined back\par quite considerably over that period," Simmonds said.\par     And, despite reports that the Bank of Korea had been\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in recent days, the scale of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 would be far lower than in the past months, he said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0918 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.85         108.36       +0.47\par  Sing dlr        1.6782         1.6805       +0.14\pa