\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Unhurried gains ahead of Greenspan.  \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2004\par 05:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, April 19 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par firmer on Monday after unexpectedly weak U.S. economic data\par soothed fears of a near-term monetary tightening there and\par caused the yen and euro to rally modestly.\par     Still, the pace of gains in the yen       , Singapore\par dollar  and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unhurried and\par reflected investor caution ahead of a Group of Seven meeting on\par the weekend and U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's\par testimony on the economy on Wednesday.\par  \par     The yen hovered around 108 per dollar, the dollar still up\par three yen from last week's lows.\par     The Singapore dollar        remained around 1.6770/80 per\par dollar, up about a cent from last week's lows, while Taiwan\par dollar  settled on the firmer side of 33 per dollar.\par     The Thai baht        was in a range of 39.30 to 39.40 per\par dollar, up a percent from last week's trough.\par     Last week's consumer sentiment and industrial production\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  data in the United States was weaker than markets expected, and   \par \par \uc2  the optimism over the economy that had driven up the   \par \par \uc2  expectations of the Fed hiking rates sooner eased.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Greenspan would also be cautious in his   \par \par \uc2  statement and would try to play down the chances of rate   \par \par \uc2  hikes.   \par \par \uc2  "Markets are probably expecting Fed chairman Greenspan to be   \par \par \uc2  measured as well, downplaying the urgency to hike interest   \par \par \uc2  rates in the near future," Jimmy Koh, analyst with United   \par \par \uc2  Overseas Bank wrote in a note.   \par \par \uc2  "Such an outcome could mean that the U.S. dollar has seen   \par \par \uc2  its high for now and could retreat to the lower end of its   \par \par \uc2  recent trading ranges."   \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the G7 meeting was probably a non-event for   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, given the perception that most Asian   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were allowing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise to ward off   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             was traded around 1,155\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar. It has risen 2.5 percent in two months, prompting\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation that the authorities have moderated their\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell in the first\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par half of April by 600 million to $162.96 billion on April 15,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said that was due to a decline in the euro\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and yen against the dollar during that period.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040419e04j000bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
