\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Recover, seen benefiting from US outlook.  \b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2004\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, April 15 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  partially\par recovered in Thursday afternoon deals after two sessions of\par weakness forced by a rallying U.S. dollar and stronger U.S.\par economic data.\par     Traders said the regionals had bottomed and firmer Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could co-exist with a stronger dollar as the\par region's export-driven economies would benefit from a U.S.\par recovery.\par  \par     The Japanese yen        was also steadier after its two\par percent fall on Wednesday to near the 109 a dollar.\par     However it remained vulnerable after reports that two more\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese civilians had been taken hostage in Iraq, not to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 mention the recent data showing an unexpectedly sharp rise in  \par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer prices and a narrowing of the huge U.S. trade  \par \par \uc2 deficit.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "We are likely to see some amount of dollar strength from\par now on," said M.R. Madhavan, a strategist with Bank of America.\par     "But Asia is still a leveraged bet on the United States and\par if the U.S. does better than Asia will do even better," he\par said.\par     The Singapore dollar        was down over two cents or over\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a percent from Tuesday's four-year peak. It fell as far as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1.6868, a two-week low, paring all the gains it made on the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 back of a surprise monetary tightening by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar weakened to 33.16 per dollar,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 down more than a percent from Tuesday's three-year highs, and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 then rallied back to 33.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Philippine peso        was marginally weaker and the\par Indonesian rupiah  fell to 8,630/8,635 per dollar.\par     Markets in Thailand were closed for the New Year holiday\par and Korean markets were shut for parliamentary elections.\par     The Indian rupee          extended losses to a two-week low\par of 43.95 per dollar.\par     On the crosses, the regionals outperformed the yen, with\par the Singapore dollar  around 64.6 yen, the highest\par the cross rate has been in a month.\par     Traders said there would be more bids for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par once markets sensed the dollar's upward momentum was easing.\par     "I think the appreciation pressure on the yen will continue\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 because the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been diluted," said Bhanu Baweja,  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS, citing Japan's deepening economic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recovery as the reason why the Japanese were comfortable with a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stronger yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The story in the rest of Asia was similar. Economic growth  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was broadening in most countries, except \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities was moderating,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 he said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0905 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       108.42         107.17       -1.15\par  Sing dlr        1.6797         1.6733       -0.38\par  Taiwan dlr      33.015         32.920       -0.29\par  Korean won     1157.00        1151.30       -0.49\par  Baht             39.65          39.23       -1.06\par  Peso             55.86          55.80       -0.11\par  Rupiah         8625.00        8600.00       -0.29\par  Rupee            43.86          43.76       -0.23\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       108.42         107.31       -1.02\par  Sing dlr   p :AAAAAAAAA\par s2J:CAAAAAAA(\par sB\par  Taiwan dlr      33.015         33.978       +2.92\par  Korean won     1157.00        1192.00       +3.03\par  Baht             39.65          39.59       -0.16\par  Peso             55.86          55.49       -0.66\par  Rupiah         8625.00        8410.00       -2.49\par  Rupee            43.86          45.60       +3.96.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040415e04f0011s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
