\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves point to less  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2004\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, April 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves hit a new record in March, but the monthly rise was only about a tenth of the gain in February, providing more evidence of a switch in policy away from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the won.  \par \par \uc2 Reserves rose by $550 million to $163.6 billion at the end of March from a month earlier, the Bank of Korea said in a statement on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 March's net increase in reserves was dwarfed by the $5.56 billion gain in February, an indication that authorities were winding down \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the won, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The smaller rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in March is attributed to the government's weakened \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the easing in the dollar against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a foreign bank trader said.  \par \par \uc2 "Authorities hardly stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the won broke through the 1,150 mark late last month", the dealer added.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won         has gained 40 won over the past month, spurred by more\par signs of economic recovery and the yen's strengthening against the\par dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It was quoted at 1,141.0 per dollar in early trade, versus Thursday's close of 1,141.2, its strongest finish since November 16, 2000.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which rarely comments on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, said reserves had been boosted by growing investment gains and a rise in dollar deposits to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by financial institutions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank operates most of its foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves in bonds and other securities that represent 77.4 percent of the total balance, with dollar deposits of financial institutions making up 22.1 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's foreign reserves at the end of March were the world's fourth largest after Japan, China and Taiwan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean reserves (US$ million):  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 End-March End-Feb End-Jan End-Dec End 2002  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 163,557 163,007 157,450 155,352 121,413.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040402e042000jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
