\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won at one-month highs, peso eases.  \b0\par\par\uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, March 17 (Reuters) - The South Korean won hit\par peaks not seen in about a month on Wednesday as Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trailed the Japanese yen's rise to a three-week high\par against the U.S. dollar.\par     The exception was the Philippine peso       . It fell to\par end local trade at 56.285 to a dollar, from an intra-day high\par of 56.20, as the market ignored comments by the country's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief.\par     Governor Rafael Buenaventura told Reuters he could probably\par avoid raising interest rates for as long as six months and that\par he expected the peso  to recover to 53-54 per dollar\par after the presidential elections in May.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers in Manila said Buenaventura's comments\par were based on assumptions that might change depending on what\par happens in the polls.\par     Opinion polls show a close fight for the presidency between\par film actor Fernando Poe Jr and incumbent Gloria Macapagal\par Arroyo.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  And dealers said the peso would stay under pressure\par until the post-election policy direction became clear.\par     "Most of the political risk has been priced in. But until\par the elections are over investors will continue to seek safety\par in dollars," said Rovic De Guzman, head of trading at the Union\par Bank of the Philippines in Manila.\par     Buenaventura also said that the next government would have\par to act immediately to narrow the perennial budget deficit. The\par government's main tax agency said on Tuesday that it had missed\par its revenue collection target in February.\par     WON ADVANCES\par     The South Korean won            rose to a high of 1,163.0\par to the dollar, its highest since February 19, defying a warning\par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that political uncertainty stemming from\par the impeachment of President Roh Moo-hyun might delay an\par already fragile recovery in Asia's fourth-largest economy.\par     "If uncertainty over the impeachment lingers, weak\par consumption and slow investment could delay economic recovery\par and hurt employment," the Bank of Korea said late on Tuesday.\par     Dealers in Singapore said the market focused on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves data showing a modest fall in holdings in the\par first half of March, providing evidence that authorities might\par be more willing to tolerate a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , like much of export-driven Asia, has been\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily to keep its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from appreciating and\par hurting competitiveness against the backdrop of the U.S.\par dollar's two-year downtrend.\par  \par     But rising global raw material prices in recent months have\par threatened to fuel inflation through costly imports.\par     A hike in interest rates, typically used to fight\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflation, is seen as hurting already weak domestic consumption  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and investment. Therefore the argument that a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 could help curb imported inflation has surfaced in recent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 comments by top South Korean finance ministry and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 officials.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But that discussion was sidelined last Friday when Roh was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 impeached by the opposition-controlled parliament for violating  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 an election law and the won fell to a one-week low of 1,181.5  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 amid fears of political turmoil.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday, South Korea's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 financial markets have largely absorbed the shock and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stabilised for the time-being.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Possibility of a wider fallout appears slim," said James  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase, in his morning  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 notes on Wednesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 El  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February surprised on the upside on strong shipments of drugs  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and electronics to Europe and Asia.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht        rose to around 39.39 per dollar, from\par Tuesday's one-week low at 39.53.\par     The Taiwan dollar          touched a two-week high at\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 33.302 per U.S. dollar. The Indonesian rupiah rose to a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-week high of 8,555.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0810 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       108.20         109.58       +1.28\par  Sing dlr        1.6985         1.7053       +0.40\par  Taiwan dlr      33.293         33.360       +0.20\par  Korean won     1164.00        1170.70       +0.58\par  Baht        