\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea says mid-March  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves down from Feb.  \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 22:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SEOUL, March 17 (Reuters) - South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves edged down for the first 15 days of March, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday, providing more evidence that\par authorities may be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less heavily in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves decreased by $483 million to\par $162.5 billion as of March 15, down from a record $163 billion\par at the end of February, as the dollar strengthened by 1.9\par percent versus the euro and 1.1 percent to the yen, the Bank of\par Korea said.\par     It said the stronger U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decreased the dollar\par value of other assets denominated in euro and the Japanese yen\par  , without elaborating on the exact asset composition.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers, however, speculate the decrease may be a\par sign that South Korea has begun loosening its grip on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, allowing a gradual appreciation of the\par won            .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     South Korea's new finance minister said early this month\par that the dollar/won exchange rate "should" be decided by the\par market and economic fundamentals, indicating market forces\par would be given more emphasis in determining won levels against\par the dollar.\par     Like other export-dependent Asian countries, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par has spent billions of dollars \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to stop\par its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rising for fear of denting exporters'\par competitiveness.\par  \par     The decrease in reserves marked the first decline after 10\par consecutive monthly rises.\par     South Korea's foreign reserves at the end of February were\par the world's fourth largest behind only Japan, China and Taiwan.\par     South Korean reserves (US$ million):\par  Mid-March   End-Feb   End-Jan   End-Dec  End 2002\par    162,524   163,007   157,450   155,352   121,413.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g002xy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
