\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Won level now no problem for Korean economy-source.   \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 23:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BASEL, Switzerland, March 7 (Reuters) - The current exchange-rate level of the Korean won poses no problem for Korea's economy, which will achieve growth of 5 percent or more this year, a Korean monetary source said on Sunday.    \par \par \uc2  Speaking to Reuters on the sidelines of a bimonthly meeting of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors from the G-10 industrialized nations and major emerging markets, the source said: "Because the yen has depreciated so much, we have some room to allow market forces to determine (the level of won). I think there is no problem with current level of the won for the Korean economy."    \par \par \uc2  "We expect that our economy will get momentum and go into a (full) recovery. I'm sure we can meet five percent or more growth this year," he added.    \par \par \uc2  Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has forecast 2004 gross domestic product of 5.2 percent after an estimated 2.9 percent in 2003. South Korea's new Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai has estimated 2004 economic growth of 5 percent to 6 percent.    \par \par \uc2  Like other Asian countries, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent billions of dollars \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in an effort to curb export-damaging appreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  Thanks to such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the won remained nearly flat against the dollar during 2003. Meanwhile, the yen and the euro gained over 10 percent and about 20 percent against the greenback, respectively.    \par \par \uc2  Upward pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the won, has eased in the past few weeks partly as expectations of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities pushed the yen down.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen hit a four-month low against the dollar beyond 110.40  last\par week while the won        stood at 1,173.00 per dollar.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040307e03700dqm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
