\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-S.Korea recovery signs grow, c/a surplus surges.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Oh Jung-hwa and Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2004\par 08:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 26 (Reuters) - South Korea's finance minister said on Thursday recovery was gathering pace in Asia's fourth-largest economy, a view seemingly endorsed by the International Monetary Fund, which raised its forecast for South Korea economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai told a weekly news conference there were increasing signs the economy had moved past its worst point.  \par \par \uc2 "The sectors are increasing where signs show the situation is improving," said Lee. "Be it a consumer sentiment index or a business survey index, indices continue to show positive signs."  \par \par \uc2 The comment comes ahead of industrial production figures due on Friday that are expected to show growth of about eight percent in January from a year earlier, marking an eighth consecutive month of gains over the year before.  \par \par \uc2 Ten economists polled by Reuters on Wednesday estimated the month's industrial output to have grown 8.0 percent on the year, although the month-on-month growth was seen slowing to 0.5 percent in January from a 2.7 percent rise in December.  \par \par \uc2 They said the anticipated slowdown in monthly growth was not seen as serious enough to hurt the generally upbeat trend in the economy as domestic consumption stages a modest recovery.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the IMF upgraded its forecast for South Korea's 2004 economic growth to 5.5 percent from 4.75 percent, reflecting views the recovery in the economy, which briefly fell into recession last year, was gathering pace.  \par \par \uc2 The revised forecast was in line with the South Korean government's expectation of between 5.0 and 5.9 percent growth and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast for a 5.2 percent gain.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday the current account surplus more than doubled in 2003 to a four-year high due mainly to record exports, and expected the balance to stay in the black for the seventh consecutive year in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The $12.3 billion surplus, and another $13.1 billion surplus in the capital account, reflected the pressure over \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won to appreciate - and the scope of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to mobilise to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cheap against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's expectation of another surplus in 2004 means that the upward pressure for the won will continue to pile up," said Lee Sang-jae, an economist at Hyundai Securities.  \par \par \uc2 Many Asian countries, whose economies rely heavily on exports that again are sensitive to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  value, have been faced with international pressure to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  move up according to the rush of capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean government has stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, contributing to a $34 billion increase in reserves to $155 billion in 2003, limiting the won's rise against a weaker dollar and keeping the average nominal effective exchange rate for the year essentially unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 The IMF also said in its annual review report South Korean authorities should allow market forces to determine the won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate by scaling back on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, which should be limited to smoothing excessive volatility.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040226e02q00175\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
