\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr hits high,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 781 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2004\par 09:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar\par touched it highest level in about 19 months on Tuesday, but\par most other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped back from recent highs on\par fears that central banks would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb exchange rate\par gains.\par     The Taiwan dollar          hit 33.075 per U.S. dollar, its\par strongest since July 2002, before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in\par to cap the rise, dealers said.\par     Dealers in Singapore said settlement of stock purchases by\par foreign investors pushed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  up. Foreign investors had\par bought over $700 million of Taiwan stocks last week, they said.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also suspected in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , where the won             touched a high of\par 1,157.0 per dollar in local trade, just shy of Friday's\par four-month high of 1,156.0 hit in offshore trade.\par     The Singapore dollar        weakened as far as 1.6783 per\par U.S. dollar before recovering, but it stayed well clear of last\par Friday's four-year peak of 1.6675.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dealers said the fall came\par after a sharp fall in the Thai baht  on Tuesday morning.\par     The baht fell to a one-week low of 39.05 per dollar amid\par talk that a foreign bank was buying U.S. dollars on behalf of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, dealers said.\par     However, rising exports and capital inflows into Asian\par equities meant the appreciation pressure on regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was expected to continue despite the efforts of central banks.\par     APPRECIATION PRESSURE\par     Peter Redward, strategist at Deutsche Bank in Singapore,\par said the upward pressure on the Taiwan dollar and South Korean\par won, on a day when the Japanese yen  eased against the\par dollar, showed the amount of capital rushing into these\par economies.\par     "Central banks have been in the market all along but the\par pressure is so much that I think on average they are now\par letting some of that pressure pass through," he said.\par     The Singapore dollar has gained almost 1.5 percent so far\par this year, against a nearly two percent rise for the whole of\par 2003. The Taiwan dollar has gained about 2.6 percent, against\par 2.2 percent in 2003, and the Korean won has risen nearly three\par percent versus a depreciation of about one percent last year.\par     Speculation of revaluation of the Chinese yuan           ,\par which is managed in a narrow range near 8.28 per dollar, and\par its potential strengthening impact on regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been another major factor attracting inflows into the region.\par     The yuan non-deliverable forward           premium on the\par three-month tenor  traded around Monday's one-month\par high of 1,400 points to the U.S. dollar.\par     The premium on the one-year tenor was around 4,600 points,\par against Monday's 4,900 points. The one-year premium hit an\par all-time high of 5,200 points in October last year.\par     At 4,600 points, the premium implies an expected\par appreciation of close to six percent against the U.S. dollar in\par a year's time.\par     A senior Chinese state official said speculation on the\par yuan has hindered plans to reform the exchange rate regime, but\par analysts said delaying an adjustment of the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was not the solution.\par  \par     "If anything, the pace of capital inflows have accelerated\par dramatically in recent weeks," Redward said.\par     The Philippine peso        edged down to hit 56.17 per\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar, even as the market in Manila speculated on the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 possibility of new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulations aimed at tougher  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 monitoring of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions by local companies.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, dealers said demand for dollars was genuine as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 companies were trying to hedge their requirements ahead of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 import season that usually begins in the second quarter.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier this month the peso hit an all-time low of 56.22  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 per dollar.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0805 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.63         105.42       -0.20\par  Sing dlr        1.6736         1.6744       +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr      33.107         33.105       -0.01\par  Korean won     1158.00        1157.50       -0.04\par  Baht             39.01          38.92       -0.23\par  Peso             56.02          56.10       +0.14\par  Rupiah         8399.00        8383.00       -0.19\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   