\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Central banks eyed, T$ at 19-mth high.  \b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2004\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar        rose\par to its highest in about 19 months on Tuesday but most Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged back from recent highs on fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb exchange rate gains.\par     The Taiwan dollar          hit 33.075 per U.S. dollar, its\par strongest since July 2002, before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in\par to cap the rise, dealers said.\par     Dealers in Singapore said settlement of stock purchases by\par foreign investors was pushing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher. They said\par while foreign investors were net sellers on Monday, they had\par bought over $700 million of Taiwan stocks last week.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also suspected in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par where the won             touched a high of 1,157.0 per\par dollar in local trade, just shy of Friday's four-month high of\par 1,156.0 hit in offshore trade.\par     The Singapore dollar        fell to 1.6775 per U.S. dollar,\par moving further away from its four-year peak of 1.6675 hit last\par week.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dealers said the move was inspired by a sharp fall in the\par Thai baht .\par     The baht fell to a one-week low of 39.04 per dollar amid\par talk that a foreign bank was buying U.S. dollars on behalf of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, dealers said.\par     However, they said rising exports and capital inflows into\par Asian equities meant the appreciation pressure on regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would continue despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     MANAGING APPRECIATION\par     James Malcolm, strategist at JP Morgan Chase in Singapore,\par said gains in Asian regionals so far this year suggested that\par central banks were only smoothing rises.\par     "It is going exactly as was expected," he said.\par     "No one said that central banks would completely get out of\par the way."\par     The Singapore dollar has gained about 1.25 percent so far\par this year, against near two percent gains in the whole of 2003.\par The Taiwan dollar has gained about 2.7 percent, against 2.24\par percent and the Korean won has risen nearly three percent\par versus a depreciation of about one percent last year.\par     Malcolm said Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation was backed by fast\par improving economic fundamentals and massive capital inflows\par that central banks would continue to manage.\par     Speculation of revaluation of the Chinese yuan           ,\par which is virtually pegged at 8.28 per dollar, and its potential\par impact on regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was another major factor\par attracting inflows into the region.\par     The yuan non-deliverable forwards           premium pulled\par back to around 1,300 points on the three-month tenor\par  , from Monday's one-month high of 1,400 points.\par     The premium on the one-year tenor was around 4,600 points,\par against Monday's 4,900 points. The one-year premium had hit an\par all-time high of 5,200 points in October last year.\par  \par     At 4,600 points, the premium implies an expected\par appreciation of close to six percent in a year's time.\par     The Philippine peso        edged down to hit 56.17 per\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, even as the market in Manila speculated on the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possibility of new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulations aimed at tougher\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monitoring of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions by local companies.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, dealers said demand for the U.S. dollar was\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par genuine as companies were trying to hedge their requirements\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the import season that usually begins in the second\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.53         105.42       -0.10\par  Sing dlr        1.6765         1.6744       -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr      33.083         33.105       +0.07\par  Korean won     1158.30        1157.50       -0.07\par  Baht             39.03          38.92       -0.28\par  Peso             56.12          56.10       -0.04\par  Rupiah         8394.00        8383.00       -0.13\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.53         107.31       +1.69\par  Sing dlr        1.6765         1.6978       +1.27\par  Taiwan dlr      33.083         33.978       +2.71\par  Korean won     1158.30        1192.00       +2.91\par  Baht             39.03          39.59       +1.42\par  Peso             56.12          55.49       -1.12\par  Rupiah         8394.00      