\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves at record high on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2004\par 04:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves reached another record in January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday, in large part a reflection of continued dollar-buying by authorities trying to prevent the won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from climbing.  \par \par \uc2 With no sign the government is weakening in its resolve to keep the won down to protect price competitiveness of exporters, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are expected to continue rising this year.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves cannot help rising for some time, given the government effort to contain the won's strength spurred by a trade surplus and foreign buying of local stocks," Ahn Byung-chan, a deputy director general of the Bank of Korea, told Reuters by telephone.  \par \par \uc2 Reserves grew $2.1 billion from a month earlier to a record $157.45 billion at the end of January, lifted by investment gains and a rise in dollar deposits of banks at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the fourth-largest in the world, rose almost $34 billion in 2003 after the government stepped repeatedly to keep the won virtually unchanged against the dollar. That sent the won plunging against the Japanese yen and the euro.  \par \par \uc2 As the economy is emerging from a brief recession last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has left interest rates at historic lows, despite concerns over inflationary pressure on rising import prices.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But heavy dollar supply from strong exports and a global trend of a\par weak dollar has put upward pressure on the won        , driving it to\par the highest level in three and a half months by noon on Tuesday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea had less than $4 billion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves at the height of the Asian financial crisis in late 1997 when the International Monetary Fund arranged a $58 billion bail-out for the country.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It repaid the last tranche of the loan in August 2001, three years ahead of schedule.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean reserves ($ billion):  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 End-Jan End-Dec End-Nov End-Oct End-Sept End-Aug  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 157.450 155.352 150.339 143.320 141.535 136.189.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040203e023000jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
