\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won ends lower on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2003\par 09:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The South Korean won             closed lower\par on the local market on Tuesday, as suspected heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par authorities to push down the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eclipsed early gains.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won ended at 1,177.5 to the dollar, off a session low of 1,178.3. It was near four-week highs of 1,172.0 in early trade after opening at 1,173.0, against Monday's close of 1,174.0  \f28 \par \par \uc2 State-run banks intensified dollar bids throughout the day, which dealers suspect were on behalf of the government, snapping a five-day winning spell for the won.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying was stronger than expected," said a local bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 A shift by foreign investors to being net sellers in the local stock market put more pressure on the won, spurring short-covering on the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "After foreign investors switched into net stock sellers, concerns over reduced supply of dollars redoubled the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a foreign bank dealer. "After the dollar rebounded as authorities expected, it looked like they made all-out efforts to push the level up further towards the close."  \par \par \uc2 Compounding the impact of government action, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement on Tuesday that it needed to consider taking countermeasures against any sharp appreciation of the won, hinting at more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities in the future.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark stock index fell 1.10 percent, with foreign investors offloading a net 51 billion won of shares.  \par \par \uc2 The won/yen cross rate , a calculated rate based on each \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value against the dollar, stood at 10.8176/35 against 10.7381/40 late on Monday, indicating the won's firmness.  \par \par \uc2 The yen was quoted at 108.80/86 to the dollar on caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the Japanese unit climbed to a three-year high of 107.82 in overnight U.S. trade.  \par \par \uc2 On the non-deliverable forward market, one-month won was quoted at 1,180.4/1.4 versus 1,176.9/7.9 late Monday and three-month won at 1,186.0/7.0 compared with 1,182.6/3.6.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Seoul Money Brokerage Service, the biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker in the country, said it had started offering electronic brokering service for non-deliverable forwards transaction from Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The computerised NDF trade, the first in the country, is expected to boost the trading volumes in the market.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031111dzbb001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
