\par\par \b \uc2 S Korea Denies  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Says Just Smoothing Ops  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hye-Seung Seo  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2003\par 04:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial authorities Wednesday denied that they recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to put a lid on the won's appreciation against the dollar and the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Kwon Tae-Shin, a deputy minister of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy, denied that Kim Jin-Pyo, who heads the ministry, told the Financial Times that the government would continue to "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to keep the won down if it rises further against the dollar and the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Kim merely said the government would conduct "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to protect the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against market volatility and speculative forces, Kwon explained.  \par \par \uc2 "The word '\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' never came up," Kwon told Dow Jones Newswires in a telephone interview.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea, which is responsible for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also said its recent efforts to bring down the won against the dollar were a form of "indirect smoothing" to alleviate outside shock, said Rhee Young-Kyun, director-general for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international department.  \par \par \uc2 He denied market speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent more than $10 billion to buy dollars via state-run banks to lift the U.S. unit from KRW1,150-levels to the current level of around KRW1,180. "That's outrageous", Rhee said when asked about the rumor during a separate telephone interview.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar gained 2.6% from KRW1,151.3 on Sept. 22, shortly after the G-7 Dubai meeting called for more flexible Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to KRW1,181.8 Tuesday. During the same period, the dollar slipped 2.5% to Y109.43 from Y112.18.  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said their smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were in accordance to international convention, and haven't prompted complaints from the U.S. or the International Monetary Fund, which monitors \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies and \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its member countries.  \par \par \uc2 But Rhee conceded the finance minister's comment on "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " could be "misleading" and could lead to complaint from the U.S. government.  \par \par \uc2 "From looking at the (FT) report, the U.S. could think we are manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The two officials also said South Korea doesn't have target levels for the won against the yen or dollar, and therefore declined comment on whether they were happy with where the won is currently trading at.  \par \par \uc2 "It's not that the government wants the won to depreciate against the yen. The decoupling of the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has happened because of market forces," said the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Kwon.  \par \par \uc2 "The fundamentals of the two countries are different. It is natural for the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go separate ways," Kwon said.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea has said it would resort to "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " if the won strengthens to a level that could undermine exports without clarifying what that level is.  \par \par \uc2 The government hopes the recent double-digit growth in exports will continue to spur economic recovery as local consumption remains sluggish.  \par \par \uc2 -By Hye-Seung Seo, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-732-2165; hyeseung.seo@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ryan Woo and Kevin Lim  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031022dzam0002a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
