\par\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Higher Late, Tracking Yen Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Ditas Lopez  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2003\par 12:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MANILA (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly up late Monday, riding on the yen which gained ahead of the corporate half-year closing, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of dollars left the New Taiwan dollar and the South Korean won flat.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said they expected more losses in the dollar-yen, with the Bank of Japan failing to make an appearance Monday, and with its quarterly "tankan" corporate sentiment survey expected to show an improvement Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 David Simmonds, senior emerging markets strategist for Asia at The Royal Bank of Scotland, said the recent Group of Seven industrialized countries' statement for more flexible exchange rates merely "helped to cement the break of the ranges" in dollar-yen and dollar-Asians. The dollar, he said, was declining and the G7 statement only accelerated the fall.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation on an early appreciation in the Hong Kong dollar have eased somewhat, but the expectation the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be revalued at some point persisted.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7485, compared with HK$7.7605 Friday, while the Hong Kong dollar forwards discount deepened, in line with the decline in the spot rate. The one-year forward was quoted at a discount of 62 to 54 to the spot rate, compared with a discount of 41 to 20 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The China yuan also ended up against the dollar, with exporters selling the dollar ahead of a weeklong holiday and to meet month-end \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements. In the spot market, the U.S. dollar closed at CNY8.2770, down from CNY8.2771 Sunday. But the bid-and-offer quote for the one-year dollar-yuan NDF stood at a discount of 3500/3350 points to the spot rate, wider than 3300/3000 late Friday afternoon. The NDFs don't have a direct influence on the spot dollar-yuan rate, but they reflect market psychology about exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 Among the gainers Monday was the Singapore dollar, which was trading around S$1.7306 to the dollar around 1010 GMT, compared with late Friday's S$1.7315. The dollar traded a range of S$1.7268 to S$1.7293 during the Asian session.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Wary Of MAS At S$1.7240/45 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A dealer at a foreign bank said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore didn't appear to be in the market although the market remains wary as the U.S. dollar nears S$1.7240/45.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's United Overseas Bank, in a report Monday, said with pressure building up on the yuan and the Hong Kong dollar, the ringgit risks being "the next rotational play. However, given the absence of an NDF market, USD/SGD is likely to be employed as proxy trade."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could effectively weaken the Singapore dollar again by tweaking the midpoint of its trade-weighted policy band, it said. "As such, USD/SGD looks trapped around 1.7250-1.7350 for the time being."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, suspected government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offset exporters' dollar sales, helping the dollar to finish unchanged from Friday's close at 1,150.5 won.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Korea Development Bank and commercial banks snapped up about $500 million on behalf of the government," a dealer at a foreign bank estimated.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's going to be hard (for the dollar) to slip below KRW1,150 with the government guarding" that level, said a dealer at a local bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also believed to have bought dollars aggressively in late trading. The U.S. dollar closed at NT$33.790, little changed from NT$33.791 Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the Philippines, the peso closed higher as some banks trimmed overbought dollar positions amid thin corporate demand early in the day and strong regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar closed at PHP54.90 on the Philippine Dealing System, down from Friday's close of PHP55.02. Volume was higher at $136.5 million from $115 million due to late buying, which traders interpret as a sign of persistent weak investor sentiment for the Philippine peso.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The risk premium on the political side is being factored in, so you have a limited upside for the peso," said a trader with local bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht, meanwhile, was stronger. The dollar closed at 40.09 baht, down from THB40.145 late Friday as offshore players focused on strong Thai economic fundamentals.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah closed slightly higher in quiet trading on speculation of further capital inflows into the local market. The dollar closed at 8,420 rupiah, down from its close Friday at IDR8,440.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said some market participants sold dollars on expectations of a rise in supply from overseas investment in Indonesian Satellite Corp.'s IDR1.75 trillion bond offering. Indosat, the country's second-largest phone company, will close book building for the bond Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ditas Lopez, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-885-0288; ditas.lopez@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Lim Mui Khi  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1136 4250  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020030929dz9t000hs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
