\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ride yen's coat-tails, but sceptical.  \b0\par\par\uc2 757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2003\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 18 (Reuters) - A surge in the yen to a\par four-month high lifted most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar\par on Thursday, but fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- despite growing\par international criticism of the policy -- limited gains.\par     Dealers said even though the yen        had strengthened\par past the crucial 116 per dollar level, few players were ruling\par out a burst of a dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of\par Japan.\par     Talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the won\par   in a narrow range, but the yen gains saw it close at\par 1,169.9 per dollar, its strongest close in local trading in\par four weeks.\par     Early \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Taiwan capped the\par local dollar at 34.068 per U.S. dollar, off Wednesday's high of\par 34.043, and it ended local trading flat.\par  \par     "We have been seeing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity across the\par region," said Thio Chin Loo, senior analyst at BNP Paribas.\par     "However the market continues to test the resolve of the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  central banks, and one view intensifying currently is that they   \par \par \uc2  will eventually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less aggressively to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strength as growth intensifies and demand picks up," she added.   \par \par \uc2  Speculation that Asian central banks would ease up on their   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has grown ahead of the weekend Group of Seven and   \par \par \uc2  International Monetary Fund meetings in Dubai, where the   \par \par \uc2  region's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is expected to be a hot topic of debate.   \par \par \uc2  U.S. and European policymakers argue that Asian   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cost their manufacturing sectors both jobs and   \par \par \uc2  markets, and has distorted the market's adjustment to a   \par \par \uc2  ballooning U.S. current account deficit.   \par \par \uc2  The IMF, in its World Economic Outlook, said the U.S.   \par \par \uc2  dollar may be in for further weakness and developing Asia was   \par \par \uc2  better equipped than Europe or Japan to bear the economic pain   \par \par \uc2  of its fall.   \par \par \uc2  DOUBTS PERSIST   \par \par \uc2  Still, some analysts were sceptical that the weekend   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "We are not looking for the G7 meeting to deliver any\par palpable results," the National Australia Bank said in a note.\par     The NAB said while portfolio inflows into Asia had been\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong, authorities remained wary of hot money and recent data,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par such as Wednesday's disappointing trade numbers from Singapore,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suggested that caution would persist.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar  struggled on the weaker side of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 1.7500 per U.S. dollar after data showed exports had posted\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a second successive monthly fall in August.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said slowing exports were likely to raise doubts\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the strength of the Singapore dollar ahead of a monetary\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy review in October. Some players believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might ease policy by targetting a weaker exchange rate.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  rose from early lows but was capped by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar purchases from foreign funds, who were still trying to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offload long baht positions.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was long of baht when last week the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Thailand slapped capital restrictions to discourage\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculative trading in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, a move which\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stemmed the momentum that had taken the baht to near three-year\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highs.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  hit a three-week low of 55.33\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar as the government confirmed that it had missed its\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par budget deficit target in August, the first overshoot of the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closely watched figure in five months.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Secretary Jose Isidro Camacho said the budget\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit was 18 billion pesos in August, more than double the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The peso closed local trade within half a peso of its\par record low of 55.75 per dollar, hit in January 2001.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        touched a near two-week low,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and dealers in Jakarta said some foreign funds were spotted\par   \f28 