\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won firmer by midday,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  concern.  \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2003\par 05:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 0300 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won firmer versus the dollar but trades in tight range, closely tracking the Japanese yen's movement in Asia trade.  \par \par \uc2 - Won briefly rises to two-week highs at one point as foreign investors keep buying local shares but retreats on concern over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finishes morning session at 1,170.4 against the dollar, compared with Monday's close of 1,171.5. It opened at a session low of 1,171.3 and touched a high at 1,169.8.  \par \par \uc2 - "The won has little room to move as fears about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to provide a floor for the dollar while the market sees steady dollar supply from equity investors," said a local bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 - Traders largely ignored the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep interest rates unchanged as the move conformed with market expectations.  \par \par \uc2 - In Tokyo, the yen is at 116.63/67 to the dollar, versus 116.83 late in New York trade on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 - Boosting the won is foreign stock buying, which has continued for 16 days in a row, raising expectations of rising dollar supply in the coming sessions.  \par \par \uc2 - The benchmark stock index up 1.38 percent.  \par \par \uc2 - Dollar offers from exporters are steady, if not massive, so far this week ahead of the September 10-12 Chusok holidays.  \par \par \uc2 - Market attention was also focused on any comments from North Korea during events marking the 55th anniversary of the communist country's foundation on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 - The won/yen cross rate , a calculated rate based on each \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value against the dollar, is at 10.0309/69 versus 10.0162/22 late on Monday, showing the won weakening.  \par \par \uc2 - On the non-deliverable forward market, one-month won quoted at 1,172.7/3.7 versus 1,173.7/4.7 late on Monday and three-month won was at 1,178.0/9.0 versus 1,179.0/80.0.  \par \par \uc2 - Seoul's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed for three days from Wednesday for public holidays.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030909dz99000mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
