\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Support From Stock Markets \b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2003\par 11:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed late Monday as stronger stock markets generally supported gains, but rises were tempered by suspected government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won ended weaker and the New Taiwan dollar finished steady. The Philippine peso drifted lower, but the Singapore dollar and Thai baht were modestly stronger. Indonesian financial markets were closed for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  Overall bids and offers were fairly well matched, which kept trading ranges tight, a trader at a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  "It's pretty mixed. There was a sell-off earlier (in the dollar versus regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), but now they (market players) are buying back. It's the same guys (who were buying and selling)," he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are underpinned by expectations of better global growth in the current half-year, led by the U.S., which is a major export market for Asia. \par \par \uc2  Hence "people are still looking to expand positions in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Bhanu Baweja, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS AG. \par \par \uc2  Security issues, which were in the spotlight recently, appeared to have been largely subsided, except in the Philippines, he said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the market is going to trade off that (security concerns) until it (something untoward) happens." \par \par \uc2  After the deadly bombing at a major hotel in Jakarta on Aug. 5, there were fears that Sunday's Independence Day celebrations in Indonesia could be a target for similar terrorist attacks, but the day passed without incident. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, some traders suspected the South Korean government had a hand in reversing the won's gains. Others said an exchange of warning shots between North and South Koreas in the afternoon also helped pushed the dollar higher. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's navy fired warning shots Monday after a North Korean fishing boat entered waters controlled by the South, the military said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 1,178.2 won, up from KRW1,176.6 at Thursday's close. The market was closed for a holiday Friday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the authorities likely bought the dollar around the intraday trough of KRW1,174. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar suddenly soared when it was just about to go below KRW1,174," said a dealer at Chohung Bank. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, resulting in the local dollar erasing early gains to close unchanged at 34.358 to the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar's initial rise was related to inflows for equity investments. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume amounted to US$450 million, up from US$433.50 million in the previous session. One dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trades may have accounted for as much as US$150 million of total volume. \par \par \uc2  "It looked like the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market a lot during the afternoon," said a foreign bank dealer in Taipei. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prefers to have the local dollar move in tandem with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of export competitors such as South Korea and Japan in order to preserve competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Both the South Korean and Taiwanese governments don't usually comment on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030818dz8i000l8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
