\par\par \b \uc2  Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; Yen's Gains Lead The Way \b0\par\par\uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2003\par 11:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened for the fourth straight session Monday, buoyed by the yen's gains against the euro and dollar. \par \par \uc2  The only exception was the Philippine peso, which weakened on dollar demand from corporations and expectations of a decline in foreign direct investment. \par \par \uc2  The yen capitalized on thin market conditions in Tokyo to climb to a three-week high against the euro, which has been retreating against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since failing to break above Y137 resistance last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Many traders in Tokyo were away from their desks for the Obon holiday. \par \par \uc2  The yen-euro rally also helped lift the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, although the U.S. unit fared better than its European counterpart. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of Asian trading the euro was changing hands at Y133.80, down from Y134.46 late Friday in New York. The dollar was quoted at Y118.67, down from Y119.04 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The yen, as it often does, sets the tone for other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar relinquished some of its gains late in the day, but held on to close stronger. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar closed at NT$34.389, down from NT$34.415 Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Bargain-hunting by some local and offshore players, as well as foreign banks, helped pull the dollar of its intraday low of NT$34.370, a trader at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The story was much the same for the South Korean won, which tracked the yen higher in lackluster trading. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 1,179.2 won, down from KRW1,181.1 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they suspected the government bought the dollar near its intraday low of KRW1,178.7 to keep a floor under the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  Authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and other Asian countries, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in an effort to curb strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The belief is that doing so will help keep their country's exports competitive based on cost. \par \par \uc2  U.S. manufacturers have complained that the practice gives their Asian competitors an unfair advantage in global markets. The U.S. General Accounting Office, the investigative arm of Congress, last week confirmed that it will review whether Asian governments are manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect exports. \par \par \uc2  Dollar purchases by Philippine importers weighed on the peso, as did weekend comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura regarding the likelihood of a slowdown in foreign direct investment. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 54.87 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from PHP54.71 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Buenaventura said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to borrow as much as $500 million in September or October to settle $115 million in debt maturing later this year, and use the balance to boost reserves in the face of the shortfall in FDI. \par \par \uc2  "Comments made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor indicate there will be a lack of dollar flows, so why should we unload now?" said a trader with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The absence of any new terrorist attacks in Indonesia provided some support for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of Asian trading the dollar was quoted at 8,540 rupiah, down from IDR8,565 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment toward the rupiah continued to improve as the market settled following last week's bombing at the Marriott Hotel in Jakarta that killed 11 people and injured 150 more. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was little changed in quiet trading. \par \par \uc2  Late in the session the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7553, compared with S$1.7555 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose in the morning after the government issued a report showing the economy shrank by 4.2% in the second quarter compared with a year earlier, slightly better than the 4.3% contraction estimated last month. \par \par \uc2  The government also lowered its full-year gross domestic product forecast to 1% growth at best, from its previous projection of a 0.5%-2.5% expansion, pushing the Singapore dollar lower in early trading. \par \par \uc2  By midafternoon profit-taking had eroded the U.S. dollar's gains, and the pair traded in a narrow range for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  The baht tracked the yen higher, showing little reaction to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official's comments that a sovereign rating upgrade was expected from Standard & Poor's Corp. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia the dollar was quoted at 41.830 baht, down from THB41.880 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  A S&P team visited Thailand recently to gather information for a regular review of the economy. The major ratings agencies all adopted a positive outlook last year on ratings equivalent to BBB- on the country's long-term foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign debt. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Simon Harvey \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030811dz8b000kx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
