\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Tentative gains as dlr weakens. \b0\par\par\uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2003\par 10:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made\par tentative gains against a weaker U.S. dollar on Monday, as the\par yen's resistance to strength, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  talk in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and Taiwan, and political risks in Philippines limited gains.\par     A mixed U.S. employment report helped the Japanese yen off\par Friday's three-month lows, but it stayed close to 120 on\par Monday.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar        was off Friday's three-month\par lows, but did not make much headway past than 1.76.\par     Traders speculated the Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  dollars, and possibly the yen, to keep the won \par \par \uc2    from firming past 1,180 and to prop the yen-won \par \par \uc2  cross rate. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar  rallied, but the fear that the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would persist with last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed. \par \par \uc2  "Central banks in the region are still actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  in the market and the dollar-yen is still hovering around 120," \par \par \uc2  said Peter Redward, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Also, investors are generally in a risk-reduction mode \par \par \uc2  after the sell-off we have seen in the fixed income markets and \par \par \uc2  the strength of the dollar, it just means that no one's \par \par \uc2  prepared to push \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around much at the moment." \par \par \uc2  Data showing a rise of $1.25 billion in Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in July strengthened the speculation that the \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea was buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  And that could increase if there is more equity inflow into \par \par \uc2  Korea after North Korea's decision on the weekend to \par \par \uc2  participate in six-way talks over its nuclear crisis, analysts \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The won has come off a 1,177 high last week and the \par \par \uc2  sensitive yen-won cross  rose to 9.85 on Monday from \par \par \uc2  a six-month low of 9.776 last week. The cross fell below 10 two \par \par \uc2  weeks ago. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Markets believe the Korean authorities are happy to see the\par cross above 10 to maintain export competitiveness with Japan.\par     Some traders said the BOK probably bought yen for won to\par prop the cross rate on Monday. Others said that was unlikely.\par     "They may buy dollar-won to move the cross. They won't risk\par the ire of the Japanese by selling dollar-yen," a trader said.\par     PESO PROPPED\par     The besieged Philippine peso        seemed to have overcome\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some of the fears of political instability and another mutiny\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as it slowly drifted away from Friday's four-month lows and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rose as far as 54.76.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It had been under pressure last week after the failed mutiny\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by hundreds of soldiers on July 27 and fell again on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid talk of unusual troop movements.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had sold dollars to ensure\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso did not fall past 55 towards a 55.16 low struck in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Redward said the Philippines' balance of payments deficit\par would keep it weak over the next few months.\par     A Philippine monetary official, who asked not to be named,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said at the weekend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was considering a dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par loan to settle $200 million in debt due in September and to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boost reserves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  made slow gains. Supported by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improving growth prospects and a rise in exports, it had not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lost much ground late last week when the U.S. dollar was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rallying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Goldman Sachs said in a report it made sense to buy options\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to sell the dollar against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially those\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with low implied volatilities such as the baht and Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could appreciate if the global activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook improves and central banks stop \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Stronger\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth, due to improved external demand, would overshadow the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par negative impact on growth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation," it said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This should support long dollar-put options in Asia."\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0806 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.88       120.33         +0.38\par  Sing dlr      1.7590       1.7636         +0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.430       34.510         +0.23\par  Korean won   1181.10      1184.00         +0.25\par  Baht           41.91        41.99         +0.19\par  Peso           54.80        54.87         +0.13\par  Rupiah       8490.00      8525.00         +0.41\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.88       118.74         -0.95\par  Sing dlr      1.7590       1.7341         -1.42\par  Taiwan dlr    34.430       34.753         +0.94\par  Korean won   1181.10      1185.80         +0.40\par  Baht           41.91        43.08         +2.79\par  Peso           54.80        53.38         -2.59\par  Rupiah       8490.00      8940.00         +5.30.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030804dz8400i26\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
