\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Stronger waiting for Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2003\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, June 25 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mostly\par stronger late on Wednesday, helped by a steady Japanese yen and\par recovering local stock markets, as markets worldwide waited for\par the U.S. Federal Reserve to announce its decision on rates.\par     And, whether or not the Fed cuts rates later on Wednesday,\par analysts said foreign portfolio inflows in search of growth and\par return would continue to seek Asian equities, putting upward\par pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Singapore dollar        managed to creep back to the\par firmer side of 1.74, coming off 1-=   month lows even as\par markets speculated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore would\par ease monetary policy next month.\par     The Thai baht        was tentative around 41.50, a level\par where markets suspect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The\par Korean won             rose after some initial hesitation\par as stocks recovered and foreign investors turned buyers again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Philippine peso        and Taiwan dollar          too\par were higher.\par     "There will be a continuing trend of capital funds coming\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par into Asia," said Karl Broecker, head of treasury at Landesbank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baden-Wuerttemberg, adding these would be into share markets in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par countries such as Thailand and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And, despite the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by central banks to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  competitive for exports, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would still gain.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Broecker said the inflows into South Korea have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overshadowed concerns of slowing growth and North Korea's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nuclear threats, and could lead the won higher to 1,180 or even\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,175. Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,180 last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Similarly, the baht would eventually overcome the\par resistance at 41.50 and move to 41.40 soon, he said.\par     RUPIAH AWAITS FLOWS, SING DOLLAR PRESSURED\par     The rupiah        was range-bound on Wednesday but traders\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said it would eventually push higher as the timing and extent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of foreign investment inflows for Bank Mandiri's initial public\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offering became clear, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The IPO for Indonesia's largest bank was subscribed 6.7\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par times, and would raise $328 million. Of this, two-thirds was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to be allotted to foreign investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, market expectations of a weakening of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar, through a shift in the trade-weighted band it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is managed in, remained high. The pressure would build if the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fed cut rates aggressively, by 50 basis points, and regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par central banks joined the race to ease policy, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "A moderate easing is very likely in Singapore," Broecker\par said.\par     "This is one tool to maintain some economic stability and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par if you see America putting short term rates below one percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par then there is the possibility of a very cautious easing and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that means the Singapore dollar could depreciate against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Yet, authorities would try to ensure the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stable and competitive against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of countries\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore competes with in export markets, such as China,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Malaysia, Hong Kong and Thailand, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0900 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.70       117.69         -0.01\par  Sing dlr      1.7397       1.7377         -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.556       34.580         +0.07\par  Korean won   1186.90      1188.70         +0.15\par  Baht           41.51        41.53         +0.05\par  Peso           53.35        53.45         +0.19\par  Rupiah       8225.00      8225.00          0.00\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End