\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; Rating Upgrade Boosts Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nirmala Menon \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2003\par 11:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- A one-notch rating upgrade for Indonesia from Standard & Poor's Ratings Services lifted the already buoyant rupiah to a 32-month peak Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed the local session at 8,430 rupiah, down from IDR8,555 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also driven higher on the back of broad U.S. dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slid against major rivals after U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said Sunday that a weaker dollar could help U.S. exports. \par \par \uc2  Snow's remarks "helped set the tone for the beginning of the week," said David Simmonds, senior emerging markets strategist for Asia at Royal Bank of Scotland. "Dollar/Asians feel heavy with the weak international dollar," and could push lower, he added. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in Asia, the dollar sank below the psychologically key Y117 level for the first time since Thursday, while the euro jumped to a fresh 52-month high of $1.1579. At 0930 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y116.65. \par \par \uc2  Government officials in Japan threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the dollar's slide. Traders said the Finance Ministry followed through on its yen-selling threat and quietly bought dollars via Japanese banks. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it isn't concerned about the dollar's fall below 8,500 rupiah as exporters can still be competitive at that level, Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was already trading at a 32-month high earlier in the session as foreign investors sold dollars to finance portfolio investment in the country. \par \par \uc2  The S&P upgrade, which came in the early afternoon, served to give a further fillip to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  S&P raised Indonesia's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to B-, from CCC+, with a stable outlook. \par \par \uc2  The agency said the move reflects the diminished likelihood that the government will seek additional debt restructuring, a situation made possible by its improving fiscal and external positions. \par \par \uc2  Simmonds said yield-hungry international investors haven't been as keen on the rupiah as other high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it isn't very liquid. \par \par \uc2  Still, "the offshore market will certainly be short dollars for carry in the appreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar briefly spiked to a two-month high, riding on the dollar's weakness and also on hopes that the SARS outbreak in the city state was well under control, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of local trading hours, the U.S. unit was quoted at S$1.7320, down from S$1.7420 late Friday, though off an intraday trough of S$1.7310, which was its lowest since early March. \par \par \uc2  Singapore hasn't reported new cases of SARS infection since April 27, and if this continues until May 18, the World Health Organization could declare the island nation as having contained the virus. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso closed at an eight-month high on the back of offshore dollar sales and remittance inflows from Filipinos working overseas, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 52.050 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, its lowest since closing at PHP51.970 on Sep. 12 last year. The dollar finished at PHP52.340 Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Amando Tetangco said the peso was boosted by overseas remittance inflows and investments - particularly portfolio investments. \par \par \uc2  Tetangco said stronger regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also aided the peso. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar followed its regional counterparts higher despite underlying concerns about the impact of the recent SARS outbreak. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit closed at NT$34.715, down from Friday's NT$34.775. Dealers said the local dollar was pulled up by a stronger Singapore dollar, South Korean won and Japanese yen. Taiwan competes with those economies in key export sectors. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan on Monday reported 23 new SARS cases - its sharpest single-day jump - bringing the total to 207. The death toll stands at 27. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fears of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market kept a check on the won's strength, market players said. \par \par \uc2  "It was range-bound trading today," said a trader. "Players are expecting a stronger Korean won but possible government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is blocking that," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped below the psychologically key 1,200 won level to end at KRW1,195.2 won, down from KRW1,200.4 Friday. \par \par \uc2  President Roh Moo Hyun's trip to the U.S. also lent some support to the won as some believe his talks with U.S. President George W. Bush this week may lead to a breakthrough in the North Korean nuclear issue. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar was quoted at 42.37 baht late in Asia, down from THB42.545 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar was well bid under THB42.40 as local importers and oil companies stepped in to buy the dollar on weakness. \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Ryan Woo \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030512dz5c000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
