\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea won turns lower on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, May 9 (Reuters) - The South Korean won         eased for the\par first time in seven trading days on Friday, with the market wary over\par possible government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warned\par growth slip below target this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won ended at 1,200.4 per dollar, versus 1,200.1 at the opening and\par Wednesday's close of 1,199.0. It moved between 1,197.5 and 1,201.6. The\par market was closed for a public holiday for Buddha's birthday on\par Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Trading was thin ahead of the weekend and because of fears about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities at around 1,200 won per dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment was cautious because the market perceived the government would keep the 1,200 threshold for now," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  In a similar fashion, the yen fell back to 117.2 yen  per dollar after hitting a 10-month high around 116 on Thursday amid speculation that Japanese authorities may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , concern about the economy revived after the Bank of Korea said the country's economic growth may fall short of its 4.1 percent target this year. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Finance Minister Kim Jin-pyo said consumer inflation would be stable for the rest of the year, but declined to comment on market speculation that an imminent interest rate cut was in the works. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee will hold its regular meeting on Tuesday to review monetary policy and decide whether to change the overnight call rate target. \par \par \uc2  Also, helping push the won lower, foreign investors turned net sellers of local shares. \par \par \uc2  However, the main KOSPI stock index  ended up 0.17 percent at 619.11 points. \par \par \uc2  Dollar supply also increased due to an inflow of foreign equity investment earlier this week, limiting the won's drop and sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to as high as 1,197.5 per dollar in the morning session. \par \par \uc2  On the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won was last quoted at 1,202.7/3.7 versus 1,199.5/1200.5 late Wednesday and the three-month won was at 1,208.1/9.1 versus 1204.7/5.7. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz5900fg0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
