\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Humbled as dollar enjoys correction. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2002\par 12:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 23 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ebbed to \par \par \uc2  multisession lows late on Tuesday as the dollar staged a \par \par \uc2  broadbased correction after its recent drop. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar rammed the euro        below parity for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first time in a week and shoved the yen to near two-week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lows beyond 117 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said players in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  consequently\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bailed out of the short dollar positions taken on worries over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the United States' ability to fund a gaping current account\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit and U.S. corporate accounting scandals that have sent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wall Street in a tailspin.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Verbal and suspected physical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities further weighed down \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore and Thailand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Growing wariness over the impact of the U.S. stock slide on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par other economies sparked an overdue correction in the massively\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par oversold dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said some U.S. funds also bought spot dollars to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par square their positions in the offshore nondeliverable forwards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market or to raise cash to meet redemptions back home.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are likely to remain volatile in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term, pulled by forces of position liquidation against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the fundamental underpinnings for a weak dollar," said Thio\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chin Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     She, however, said the dollar may not be able to draw\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support on this short liquidation rally for long.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Trade cautiously, with a view to re-establish short dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions at higher levels," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 ended onshore trade at 1,173.1,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par just shy of the 1,174 session low. It closed on Monday at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,165.60, the highest level in 20 months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     State banks were spotted buying dollars which exacerbated\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar demand from offshore players and sent exporters on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sidelines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht dropped by about one and a half percent to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par touch lows beyond 41 per dollar, for the first time in over a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said he was feeling more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comfortable with the level of the baht after its decline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "At today's level of 40.70 baht, we are quite comfortable,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as it (baht) is stabilising while the dollar is strengthening,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Thailand's chief Pridiyathorn Devakula said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar slipped through the 1.7400 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar level to a trough of 1.7480, its lowest point in over a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, as state names were spotted selling dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar          fell to 33.294 per dollar before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closing onshore trade at 33.289. It closed on Monday at 33.028.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Fresh economic data also failed to provide any support to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Taiwan dollar with both export orders and industrial output\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for June growing at levels below market expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        ended onshore trade at 50.66,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against Monday's 50.38, tracking the regional mood and after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the government said it had overshot its six-month deficit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par target by some 53 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The number is keenly watched by financial markets as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par signal of the government's fiscal efficiency.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Department of Finance said the six-month deficit came\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in at 119.72 billion pesos, against a target of 78.26 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pesos. That raised doubts the Philippines would be able to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the deficit within the 130 billion whole year target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah fell past 9,000 per dollar to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hit a session low of 9,020, more than two percent off against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Monday's 8,810.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0945 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.66       116.22         -1.22\par  Sing dlr      1.7467       1.7346         -0.69\par  Taiwan dlr    33.289       33.028         -0.78\par  Korean won   1173.10      1165.60         -0.64\par  Baht           40.95        40.38         -1.39\par  Peso           50.39        50.38         -0.02\par  Rupiah       9000.00      8810.00         -2.11\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.66       131.24        +11.54\par  Sing dlr      1.7467       1.8515         +6.00\par  Taiwan dlr    33.289       34.986         +5.10\par  Korean won   1173.10      1277.00         +8.86\par  Baht           40.95        44.16         +7.84\par  Peso           50.39        51.50         +2.20\par  Rupiah       9000.00     10350.00        +15.00\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020723dy7n00kol\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
