\par\par \b \uc2  Korea won ends touch lower on verbal  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2002\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, July 11 (Reuters) - The South Korean won -closed slightly weaker against the dollar on Thursday, weighed down by a barrage of verbal and direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities. \par \par \uc2  The won settled at 1,179.5 per dollar against Wednesday's close of 1,179.4. \par \par \uc2  It opened at 1,178.5 and moved between 1,171.5 and 1,183.5. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said state-run banks and other lenders bought dollars worth $300 million, following repeated verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official at the Finance Ministry said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's instability was excessive and the government would stabilise the market. \par \par \uc2  The won has gained more than 10 percent in the past three months, spurred by South Korea's improving economic fundamentals, weakness in the U.S. dollar and a strengthening Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also expressed concerns about the won's steep rise. \par \par \uc2  "It is natural to take steps when the market loses stability," said an official at the Bank of Korea. \par \par \uc2  But the won's fall was capped by steady dollar selling by exporters such as automakers and electronics makers around 1,180 won per dollar.. \par \par \uc2  Dealers agreed that the timing of the government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was apt, but they were mixed over how long the effects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would last. \par \par \uc2  "The government may be able to adjust the won's strengthening pace, but the upward trend is likely to continue, testing the government will," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "It would be hard for the authorities to keep pressure on the won when the yen keeps going up," he said. \par \par \uc2  The won tends to shadow the yen due to the overlapping export items of the two countries such as electronics, shipbuilding and automobiles. \par \par \uc2  The greenback continued to fall against the yen on concerns over U.S. accounting practices and Wall Street losses. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at a 10-month low of 117.35/38 yen . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market shrugged off the latest cabinet shakeup in which President Kim Dae-jung replaced the prime minister and six other ministerial posts ahead of presidential elections in December. \par \par \uc2  On the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won was traded at 1,182.0/3.0 per dollar against 1,179.6/80.6 late Wednesday. The three-month won was at 1,187.6/8.6 against 1,185.2/6.2. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020712dy7b00e2c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
