\par\par \b \uc2  Korea bonds end mixed as investors stay on sidelines. \b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2002\par 10:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SEOUL, May 28 (Reuters) - South Korea's bellwether bond \par \par \uc2  prices ended mixed on Tuesday as many investors remained on the \par \par \uc2  sidelines awaiting the release of key economic data this week to \par \par \uc2  provide further direction for the fixed income market. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark three-year treasury bond yield finished up one \par \par \uc2  basis point at 6.32 percent, while the yield on five-year \par \par \uc2  treasuries was flat at 6.75 percent. \par \par \uc2      "Trading volume was light as a listless mood continues in the \par \par \uc2  bond market," said a fixed income trader at Hyundai Investment \par \par \uc2  and Securities. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                             close      prev close\par     * 5-yr treasury bonds                   6.75 pct    6.75 pct\par     * 3-yr treasury bonds                   6.32 pct    6.31 pct\par     * 3-yr corporate bonds                  7.08 pct    7.08 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * 2-yr monetary stabilisation bonds     6.12 pct    6.12 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * 1-yr treasury bonds                   5.46 pct    5.46 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * 1-yr monetary stabilisation bonds     5.46 pct    5.46 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * 3-mth CDs                             4.83 pct    4.83 pct\par     * Average interbank call                4.40 pct    4.40 pct\par     * Average call rate                     4.25 pct    4.15 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NOTE - Data from the Korea Securities Dealers Association and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea Money Broker Corp. Call average as of 0730 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said the won's steep rise emerged as a factor that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could dampen bond market sentiment, since government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would put pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to issue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stabilisation bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears of government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have risen since Finance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Minister Jeon Yun-churl expressed on Monday concerns about the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won's steep rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors were awaiting the government's release of April\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par industrial output figures on Wednesday and May consumer price\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea's industrial output grew 3.7 percent month on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month in March thanks to stronger demand for semiconductors and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par autos. March's output marked a swift recovery from a surprise 3.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent drop in February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea's consumer price index in April rose at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par faster-than-expected 0.6 percent month on month, led by rising\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par oil prices, with economists saying inflation was likely to build\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further in a presidential election year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, there was a lack of direction from the U.S. bond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, which was closed on Monday for the Memorial Day holidays,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Korea (BOK) sold 1.5 trillion won ($1.23\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion) in 546-day monetary stabilisation bonds (MSBs) on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday at a yield of 5.88 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the Korea Futures Exchange, the key September contract on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par three-year treasuries closed down three ticks at 103.95, while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the September contract ended down three ticks at 103.07.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ($1=1218.8 won).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020528dy5s00hrc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
